---
# clang-tidy config, agreed 2026-08-21. Goal: a routinely-clean lint pass
# that surfaces real defects (narrowing conversions, precedence bugs,
# actual modernization) without noise from checks that fight this
# codebase's own established, deliberate conventions.
#
# Whole families excluded outright (house styles or platforms irrelevant
# to this project -- Linux/x86_64 only, plain C++17, no Google/LLVM/
# Android/Apple/embedded/kernel target): google-*, llvm-*, fuchsia-*,
# android-*, objc-*, darwin-*, zircon-*, altera-*, llvmlibc-*, openmp-*,
# mpi-*, boost-*, abseil-*. cert-*/hicpp-* excluded too -- both are
# almost entirely aliases of bugprone-*/cppcoreguidelines-* checks under
# different names; enabling them alongside bugprone-* just reports the
# same finding twice. cppcoreguidelines-* excluded wholesale (its
# defaults assume an owning-raw-pointer/RAII-everywhere style this
# project's bounds-checked-parsing code doesn't follow) except for
# narrowing-conversions, pulled in via its bugprone-* alias instead.
#
# Individually excluded, with reasons (see this project's own CLAUDE.md
# for the "why" convention these follow):
#   readability-identifier-length: this codebase deliberately uses short
#     names in tight, well-scoped loops (i, n, ts, v) -- clang-tidy's
#     default 3-char minimum fights that on sight.
#   modernize-use-trailing-return-type: never used anywhere in this
#     codebase; enabling it would flag literally every function.
#   readability-braces-around-statements: this codebase's own style
#     allows an unbraced single-line `if (x) return;` -- see e.g.
#     m2_animation.cpp's own such lines throughout.
#   readability-magic-numbers / readability-uppercase-literal-suffix:
#     this is a binary-format parser -- named byte offsets/sizes/masks
#     are already the norm where it matters; blanket-flagging every
#     literal (0x0C, 4, 12, ...) in offset arithmetic would drown real
#     signal.
#   readability-else-after-return / readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator:
#     stylistic-only, no real defect signal, would just create churn
#     across guard-clause-heavy parsing code that already reads clearly.
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once: this project targets Linux/x86_64
#     only (see nix/flake.nix's own `platforms`) and already uses
#     `#pragma once` everywhere -- the check exists for cross-compiler
#     portability this project doesn't need.
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: checked against real output --
#     fires on ~15+ existing `(const std::string&, const std::string&, ...)`
#     signatures throughout src/, all named clearly at every real call
#     site (`--db2-dir`/`--dbd-dir`-shaped flag-resolution functions,
#     mostly) -- restructuring all of them (wrapper types, reordered
#     params) for marginal swap-safety isn't worth the churn this session.
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity: this project's own
#     foreign-data parsing style is deliberately long, linear,
#     "one field -> one check -> one destination" functions (see
#     CLAUDE.md's Foreign Data policy) -- splitting a correct, linear
#     parse function into artificial sub-functions purely to satisfy a
#     complexity score fights that convention rather than serving it.
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion: checked against real output --
#     100% `if (ptr)`/`if (count)` truthiness checks, the standard modern
#     C++ idiom this codebase uses throughout; requiring `!= nullptr`/
#     `!= 0` everywhere would be a step backward in style, not forward.
#   readability-isolate-declaration: real but purely cosmetic (`uint16_t
#     c0, c1;`-style multi-declarations, 16 sites) -- no defect signal,
#     left for a future pass if wanted rather than bundled into this one.
#   readability-math-missing-parentheses: checked against real output --
#     all 116 hits are `+`/`-` mixed with `*` (e.g. `offset + i * stride`,
#     this codebase's single most common binary-offset idiom), the one
#     precedence rule with essentially zero real-world ambiguity risk;
#     the check's real value (catching e.g. `a & b == c`) never triggered
#     once in this codebase.
#   performance-enum-size: real but low-value here -- every flagged enum
#     (FieldCompression, ColumnKind, ColumnType, State, AlphaMode) is a
#     small in-memory value, never stored at scale; the byte savings
#     don't justify the per-enum ABI-safety review needed before shrinking
#     one already crossing static_cast<uint32_t>() boundaries with real
#     file data.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  modernize-*,
  readability-*,
  -google-*,
  -llvm-*,
  -llvmlibc-*,
  -fuchsia-*,
  -android-*,
  -objc-*,
  -darwin-*,
  -zircon-*,
  -altera-*,
  -openmp-*,
  -mpi-*,
  -boost-*,
  -abseil-*,
  -cert-*,
  -hicpp-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -readability-else-after-return,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses,
  -performance-enum-size
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
FormatStyle: none
